00:01:54.844 --> 00:01:59.304
Warren Buffett's long record at Berkshire Hathaway is the reminder that bear markets do

00:01:59.304 --> 00:02:04.224
not have to stop compounding when the focus stays on business quality, according to analysis

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:05.304
from the Motley Fool.

00:02:05.964 --> 00:02:10.844
Valuation discipline treats a depressed multiple as a volatility buffer when momentum names

00:02:10.844 --> 00:02:11.924
rotate out of favor.

00:02:11.924 --> 00:02:16.944
A broader market pullback is the tape where low price to earnings names can absorb swings

00:02:16.944 --> 00:02:18.464
better than high growth peers.

00:02:19.104 --> 00:02:25.284
The S&amp;P 500 has advanced on artificial intelligence or AI excitement for three years, yet Buffett

00:02:25.284 --> 00:02:29.244
still treats temporary declines as normal rather than a reason to panic sell.

00:02:29.844 --> 00:02:34.444
On your broker platform, screen for stocks trading below their five-year average price to

00:02:34.444 --> 00:02:35.224
earnings ratio.

00:02:35.644 --> 00:02:40.404
Then run that list inside a TFSA so the tax wrapper is decided before the click.

00:02:40.404 --> 00:02:45.064
Crosse checks same-day volume against the 20-day average before treating any

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:50.304
bounces confirmed. That pairing held up best during the 2022 rate hike stretch

00:02:50.304 --> 00:02:55.184
when value cushioned the drawdown while growth corrected sharply. The risk is

00:02:55.184 --> 00:02:58.864
that prolonged outflows can keep those multiples compressed longer than a

00:02:58.864 --> 00:03:03.144
weekly hold can wait. Stay with underlying earnings power rather than headline

00:03:03.144 --> 00:03:08.435
volatility if the aim is the market's long-term upward drift. Trade web markets

00:03:08.435 --> 00:03:14.315
Its ticker TW stays on the monitor as a simulated volume confirmation play in NASDAQ financials,

00:03:14.695 --> 00:03:15.955
with no new entry today.

00:03:16.415 --> 00:03:21.655
This is a simulated trade for learning purposes using no real money, and the figures come via

00:03:21.655 --> 00:03:22.735
simply wall-steed.

00:03:23.075 --> 00:03:28.275
The catalyst already on the tape is September average daily volume of $81.6 trillion.

00:03:28.915 --> 00:03:36.235
Third quarter volume printed $210.3 trillion, with average daily volume up 29% year over

00:03:36.235 --> 00:03:40.195
year for that September print, and 22.4% for the quarter.

00:03:40.795 --> 00:03:45.355
Price has been sitting above the 20-day moving average, which is the technical half of the

00:03:45.355 --> 00:03:45.655
setup.

00:03:46.275 --> 00:03:50.795
Expense growth and technology spend could compress margins if throughput does not convert

00:03:50.795 --> 00:03:54.515
into fees, so the plan stops its 8% below entry.

00:03:55.095 --> 00:04:01.595
The weekly target is plus 2% to plus 4% over 5 sessions if the volume trend holds, and confidence

00:04:01.595 --> 00:04:04.915
is medium because sector rotation headwinds are still in the tape.

00:04:04.915 --> 00:04:11.315
In validation is the line to copy, September average daily volume growth falling below 15%

00:04:11.315 --> 00:04:15.635
year over year on the next reported month would kill the thesis before more capital is

00:04:15.635 --> 00:04:16.575
imagined at risk.

00:04:16.995 --> 00:04:21.015
You have a confirmed throughput print and rotation still chewing on growth names.

00:04:21.555 --> 00:04:23.215
Do you fill anyway or do you wait?

00:04:23.815 --> 00:04:28.695
The volume confirmation rule and the valuation discipline screen are why there is no simulated

00:04:28.695 --> 00:04:29.315
fill today.

00:04:29.875 --> 00:04:34.155
The print is on the board and the volume filter still has to clear when cash markets are

00:04:34.155 --> 00:04:39.955
actually open. No simulated hold reached a scheduled Friday evaluation since the last review,

00:04:40.435 --> 00:04:45.275
so there is no new realized result to read. The most recent practice investment has already

00:04:45.275 --> 00:04:51.625
been marked, and anything still open stays pending its five-session window. Trade Web was never filled,

00:04:51.805 --> 00:04:57.005
which means there is no Monday open, no Friday close, and no weekly percentage to grade against

00:04:57.005 --> 00:05:02.745
the NASDAQ over a matching hold. A five-session clock only starts at the next open after an actual

00:05:02.745 --> 00:05:06.505
simulated entry, and that entry is still waiting on the volume filter.

00:05:07.065 --> 00:05:11.585
The thesis on electronic trading throughput has not been invalidated, because the next

00:05:11.585 --> 00:05:13.365
monthly volume print has not arrived.

00:05:14.005 --> 00:05:18.525
Rotation through growth and financials can still change the setup before a fill, which

00:05:18.525 --> 00:05:20.825
